                <pb facs="0060" n="46" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg46"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/3811: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-28T11:00:00+07:00">March 28, 1944—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 28—10:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>539. Under date March 24, Embassy telegraphed Drumright at Sian (1) to keep us
                    currently advised all pertinent information he could obtain (our 485, March 18
                    and last paragraph 497, March 21;<anchor n="14" xml:id="d40-f1"/> (2) to keep in
                    touch with Americans in areas which might be threatened with view to advising
                    them, if circumstances should warrant, to withdraw in ample time to safer
                    places. He replied under date March 25 he was advising American missionaries
                    Chengchow area, also Hsuchang and Chowkiakow, Honan, to withdraw and stated he
                    felt all Americans should be formally advised to retire from Anhwei and Honan
                    Provinces. Embassy telegraphed approval March 26 and is so informing mission
                    offices here requesting that they notify their missionaries to leave those
                    areas.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
